{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793624139,"nonce":"fTeX9z261wsoGbdaprtsYvMObKw=","title":"No CSS scrollbar-color: scroll bars are coloured only from Rust","message":"A scroll widget's thumb and track colours live in its physics config (Scroll::scrollbar_thumb_color / scrollbar_track_color) and nothing in the stylesheet reaches them. cn::scroll_area therefore still picks its defaults from ColorToken in Rust (thumb --border at half alpha, track --surface at a tenth), the last piece of 5c464d0 that cannot move to a rule.\n\nWanted: the standard scrollbar-color: \u003cthumb\u003e \u003ctrack\u003e property parsed into ElementStyle and applied to the scroll config when the element is styled (base and state rules), with the Rust setters as inline overrides that win. Then .cn-scroll-area carries the defaults.","files":null}]}